  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Postharvest Value Chain Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve the Georgia fruit and nuts postharvest value chain by providing training and individual consultancy on skills, technology and best practices of sorting, grading, storing and packing produce. It will improve product quality and give companies the skills to add more value to the products. Participants will be cold storage and consolidation centres and food processing companies.Within this value chain, the focus is on companies active in almond and walnut processing and packing, fruit, berry or vegetable freezing and drying, cold-pressed fruit and vegetable juices, low or no-sugar jams and preserves. This project contributes to the USAID Agriculture programme and is a companion to the PSD Toolkit project PKB20GE01, Nursery Development Georgia.</narrative>
  </description>
